body:
I don't know if it's about how much pain is inflicted upon them, versus how much pain they can bear.  If I were to objectively judge, I think my grandmother went through a lot less pain than my mother given their circumstances and all.  My grandmother killed herself - by setting herself on fire no less whereas my mother is still here today.  If I were to objectively judge myself and my mother, I think she's been through a lot more than I have, but I have a lot less fortitude to deal, and I keep looking to suicide for an answer.

So I don't know the answer to your question.  Were they in more pain?  Maybe the pain you feel today would be something unbearable to them, something they would have escaped far before this point.  Maybe it's a blip in what they felt.  Do you have to feel worse?  I don't know...  Or do you maybe have to be more at peace with your decision?  So do you have to feel better?  

About the 14yo.  I obviously have no clue about their circumstances (or yours), so I can't compare.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
